  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Docudays UA  &#x2013; International Documentary Human Rights Festival</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Docudays UA  &#x2013; International Documentary Human Rights Festival</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rslaget r&#xf6;r st&#xf6;d till den 14:e | * 4 grader * | 24-31 mars 2017 och 15:e | * K&#xf6;n * | 23-30 Mars 2018 | DocudaysUA Human Rights Documentary Film Festival. Festivalen &#xe4;r i linje med den svenska regeringens regionala resultatstrategi 2014-2020. Festivalen kompletterar och ger synlighet till annat arbete av Sida inom omr&#xe5;det m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter i Ukraina.

Efter att ha skapat en plattform f&#xf6;r en MR-fokuserat samh&#xe4;llsdialog genom festivalerna som skall h&#xe5;llas i Kiev kommer DocudaysUA Festival att resa till &#xf6;ver hundra st&#xe4;der och byar och n&#xe5; en &#xe5;rlig publik p&#xe5; 100 000 &#xf6;ver hela landet. Festivalen kommer att inneh&#xe5;lla diskussioner, seminarier, rundabordskonferenser, presskonferenser och utbildningar. Insatsen har ett interaktivt format, mycket l&#xe4;mpligt f&#xf6;r att leverera politiska budskap i linje med Sveriges prioriteringar i Ukraina.

Standardrisker f&#xf6;r insatsen &#xe4;r medelh&#xf6;ga / h&#xf6;ga. De h&#xf6;gsta riskerna &#xe4;r kopplade till finansiell kontroll, upphandling, korruption samt m&#xf6;jligheterna att uppn&#xe5; h&#xe5;llbara resultat. Ambassaden kommer att godk&#xe4;nna &#xe5;rlig budget samt arbetsplan. Sidas upphandlingsregler kommer att anv&#xe4;ndas.

Den svenska ambassaden v&#xe4;ntar p&#xe5; inkommandet av en revision f&#xf6;r insatsen 55070079.

Aktivitetsperioden &#xe4;r 2017/01/01 - 2018/12/31.
Avtalsperioden &#xe4;r 2017/01/01 - 2019/09/30.

*************</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposal concerns support to the 14th | *4 Degrees*| 24-31 March 2017  and 15th |*Gender*| 23-30 March 2018| DocudaysUA Human Rights Documentary Film Festival. The festival is fully in line with the Swedish Government Regional Results Strategy 2014-2020. The festival complements and gives visibility to other work by Sweden in the area of human rights in Ukraine.

After providing a platform for a HR-focused societal dialogue, initially held in Kyiv in March 2017 and March 2018, the DocudaysUA Festival will travel throughout Ukraine to over a hundred Ukrainain cities and villages to engage with an 100 000-wide audience throughout the country annually. The festival will include discussions, petitions, seminars, round tables, press-conferences, master classes. The contribution has, therefore, an interactive format, very suitable for delivering policy messages in line with the priorities of Sweden in Ukraine.

The standard risks for the intervention are medium high / high. The highest risks are connected to the financial control, procurement, corruption and failure to sustain results. The Embassy shall approve annual budgets and work plans. Sida&apos;s procurement rules will be used.  

The Embassy of Sweden is awaiting an audit for the Contribution 55070079.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrainian society, both members of the public and duty bearers, are better aware of human rights and universal values enshrined in international and regional HR conventions</narrative>
  </description>
